                <pb facs="1544" n="1386" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1386"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Jay to
                        Consul-General Bergholz</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring closing Mahardeh school matter has been actively taken up with Porte,
                    which promised to send telegraphic instructions to vali to reopen school and not
                    interfere with schools without special orders from here, but it expressed doubts
                    if it is genuine American institution.</p>
                <p>These instructions will probably not reach Vali for several days, therefore
                    please telegraph result Thursday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
